@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+HOST-ONLY DRAFT — not enabled, not hardware-qualified.
+Base framework commit d89e00a103772f803f760979aabf8145e7731e1b.
+Only exact LDY-AN00/ldy_an00 default provider can select this adapter; resource opt-in defaults false.
+Local standard V3 interface/hash represents implemented standard V3 operations. OEM V2/hashbcc6aa... is separately runtime-gated. This is not a generated/reconstructed OEM AIDL identity claim.
+The factory hook covers metadata and reconnect. asBinder returns original remote IFingerprint/ISession handles for existing provider death linkage.
+Only typed standard operations and fixed enrollment TP feature2,1,1/1,0 are sent. Original HAT/cancellation/callback values forwarded. Native strength/enrollment limit left unchanged. No callback/service registration collision, daemon, broad command endpoint, vendor ELF/bootchain patch or private template migration.
+
+Evidence under artifacts/fingerprint-stock-reference:
+ original-honor-fingerprint-parcelers.txt (JavaV1 older contract)
+ honor-v2-ndk-full-disassembly.txt + relocations (actualV2: standard1..20, append33/34)
+ stock-touchscreen-aidl-contract.txt + tp-v1-ndk-disassembly.txt (actualTPV1/hash842c...)
+ stock-honor-fingerprint-client-callbacks.txt + stock-touch-enrollment-hook.txt
+ MINIMAL-SOURCE-BRIDGE-PROPOSAL.txt + NATIVE-ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW.txt
+
+Enrollment cleanup:
+ Actual small lease class host-tested for failed enable, failed cleanup, idempotence, expiry and reacquisition refusal.
+ TP mode is acquired only when enrollment is requested; no startup TP setter.
+ Failed cleanup retains process-wide owner and blocks further acquisition.
+ Own-session error/progress0/cancel/close/death restores TP mode; an old session cannot clear another session owner.
+ 120s watchdog uses a per-acquisition generation, marks that session expired and attempts TP cleanup. It does not fabricate biometric callbacks, a successful cancellation or an authentication result.
+ Synchronous Binder acquisition/calls themselves can stall, including while synchronized; deadline is a cleanup trigger, NOT a hard bounded completion guarantee.
+ Standard AIDL biometric scheduling guarantees one in-flight operation and terminal callback ordering. Same-session arbitrary delayed duplicate terminal callbacks have no request token and cannot be independently disambiguated here. Do not claim recovery from arbitrary vendor protocol violations.
+ A newly-created remote session is closed if its identity/death-link setup fails, only if the expected session descriptor is present. Cleanup failure is recorded, not called proven release.
+
+Qualification so far:
+ Standalone cachedJDK21 javac against actual existing framework header jar + ONLY temporary new-resource-ID stub passed for actual factory+adapter+lease. This is NOT normal Soong/resource/policy qualification.
+ Actual lease Java host tests19 assertions passed; fake setter outcomes do not prove Binder/SELinux/TP/physical behavior.
+ No source main/OUT integration, phone setter/enrollment/install/reboot or firmware trial performed.
+ Still required: reviewed radius/location overlay and exact display-default provenance; actual combined-policy system_server TP-client membership (stock puts it in system_ext, not vendor); source-level callback/transport review; normal Soong/resources/neverallows; actual final-image extraction/policy checks; separately authorized hardware enrollment/auth tests.
+ Config false must remain until those enablement gates are closed. This is actual transport/lifecycle code, not a claim that feature XML or a geometry override alone fixes the stock CTS endpoint.
+
+Geometry revision:
+Runtime WMS getInitialDisplaySize AND getBaseDisplaySize must both equal1216x2640. ro.config.default_screensize must be empty or exactly1216,2640, conservatively excluding a conflicting MTK override regardless the ROG enable flag. Checked on connect, metadata lookup, session creation and six operation-start methods; cleanup/cancel/close remain available on mismatch.
+Production pure guard host tests14assertions verify each dimension, rotation, missing values and conflicting/malformed override refusal. This simulates WMS returnvalues; actual WMS reads not executed in this host preparation.
+Exact stock DTBO SHA648b539dcfd1eec58571101ae7a33a07c40c6914f744a2b5aa4ed53526aaaf4d, all10variants same product113,type304,corners440/712..560/766,radius72; bothproduct113properties validated pervariant.
+Original Java physicalConvert2Px26f170 uses Math.round percorner then original controllerintegeraverage ->608,1951. DTSradius72→nativecmd902132310→stockgetHighLightspotRadius26e7d8→setHighLightSpotRadius25d62c→setRadius2610e4→CanvasdrawCircle260f74. OriginalgetPxScale257bfc=current/defaultdisplayheight; radius72nativepixels atscale1. A separate58dp logo fallback is not used as sensor radius. OEMdisplay method266a74→2992d4 mode0initial,1base;2984b8MTKoverride usesro.config.default_screensize.
+Source module/geometry assets staged in separate devicechild; normal Soong/resources/policy/finalimage checks still required. Product opt-in selection for host candidate can follow source qualification; installation/enrollment requires separate reviewed trial approval. No hardware functional PASS is claimed.
