@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+LDY-AN00 authentication touch-mode candidate (UNMERGED / HARDWARE UNTESTED)
+
+Stock proof: artifacts/honor-v13-preparation/fingerprint-auth-failure/stock-auth-touch-review/RESULT.json
+SHA256 d41b3b94a4d4bb3f47dce047897ebaccd8301d89defa0dd0f58ed0c113bb492c.
+The stock AuthenticationClient lifecycle requests the private TP feature2 "1,1",
+and releases it with "1,0"; enrollment had this prerequisite, authentication did not.
+The owner-locked attempt trace (SHA256
+2a2fdf88e1eb1054da63ba103d2f0f1be8e69ef4fd2b9ece322394f070eb6a50)
+showed14 DOWN events reaching native with no authentication match/fail.
+
+Scope: existing private adapter auth4/15 and enrollment3/16 share one process-wide
+TP lease. Detect5/17, sensor geometry/strength/IDs, HATs, templates, pointer payloads,
+standard/OEM interface identity checks and forwarded callback payloads are unchanged.
+No enrollment or keyguard UI, coordinates, PIN, TEE or provisioning change.
+
+The lease reserves a unique operation token before TP enable. TP setter and native
+start/cancel/close RPCs and forwarded callbacks run outside all state monitors.
+An enable-in-flight terminal defers disable until enable returns. Failed cleanup
+retains global ownership and blocks new acquisition. Old captured cancellation and
+timeout tokens cannot disable a later lease; an old cancellation also cannot invoke
+a reused native cancellation signal. Native call reservations prevent reuse before
+an outstanding owned start/cancel/close returns. Close cannot overtake an owned
+pending start: it is deferred until the start frame finishes, while keeping its
+reservation. Immediate close errors still propagate; deferred errors are logged
+and fenced, with no fabricated onSessionClosed callback.
+
+Authentication has NO120-second deadline. Ordinary onAuthenticationFailed forwards
+unchanged and retains TP mode for another attempt. Success/result-success/error/
+lockout/session-close/death terminate the operation. Cancel return alone and an
+enrollment deadline request TP cleanup, but do not prove native quiescence: another
+acquisition remains fenced until the native terminal or session close/death.
+Enrollment alone retains its120-second cleanup deadline and expired-session fence.
+
+The OEM session callback carries no operation ID. Captured local cleanup, timeout,
+and cancel ownership is protected; arbitrary unsolicited/duplicate OEM terminal
+callbacks after an acknowledged terminal and subsequent session reuse cannot be
+perfectly attributed. Normal scheduler and native callback ordering remain a
+protocol assumption. Tests must not be called proof of generic late OEM callbacks.
+Binder calls remain synchronous: there is no hard completion-time bound for a hung
+TP/HAL service. No monitor-held RPC or waiting on callback threads was introduced.
+
+Host test (actual pure production helper; not Android Binder/hardware):
+  javac -d /tmp/private-output \
+    core/java/android/hardware/fingerprint/LdyAn00FingerprintTouchMode.java \
+    core/tests/host/ldy_an00_fingerprint/TouchModeHostTest.java
+  java -cp /tmp/private-output android.hardware.fingerprint.TouchModeHostTest
+Use a fresh output on the authorized build server; do not run this on a phone.
+Tests exercise admission, failure cleanup, captured stale cancellation, callback
+reentrancy during enable, deferred close/start ordering and native-call fences.
+Adapter source checks and cached-header compilation are separate, bounded evidence.
+Normal Android framework build, actual-image ABI/policy checks and a separately
+authorized owner authentication/cancel/lockout/session-switch test remain required.
